From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dariusz Majnert <dariusz.majnert@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:52:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] motion: allow concurrent individual joint homing

Differences on pre2: upstream's bounded homing moves return a joint to
the start of its move through the joints of the running sequence, which
an independent home is not part of; home_return_group() treats an
independently homed joint as its own group so its return completes and
leaves other homes alone. homecomp.comp gains the matching changes in its
skeleton and custom variants and exports get_home_sequence_is_active(),
which motmod requires. Upstream's aggregate homing_active status carries
the "active until the last joint finishes" flag to task, so a G28.2 Pn
now waits for all concurrent homes. Availability acquisition issues its
home through task's queued G28.2 path; it cannot start while any homing
is active and blocks other HOME requests while in progress, as before,
so the new concurrency checks never refuse it.
